# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Overworld
composer Claude
about    Out under the open sky with the road ahead: a slow flute tune in D over harp and strings, with a Mixolydian C and a Bb in the middle. When something is near the tune falls away to toms, timpani and a shaker; it comes back with the kit when the thing comes for you, and hand it to horn and choir for a guardian.
tempo    92
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.35

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead harp strings tuba glock
# mood treasure: harp strings glock wonder
# mood sense:    toms timpani shaker pulse strings glock
# mood rise:     sense lead harp tuba kick snare
# mood fight:    rise -harp -glock horn brass crash
# mood boss:     fight -lead choir gong

voice lead     flute     vol=0.9  pan=-0.1
voice horn     horn      vol=0.6  pan=0.2  oct=-1
voice brass    brass     vol=0.4  pan=-0.25 gate=0.8 center=E4
voice harp     harp      vol=0.5  pan=0.3
voice strings  strings   vol=0.3  pan=-0.3 center=A3 att=0.4 rel=0.8
voice tuba     tuba      vol=0.7  gate=0.9
voice glock    glock     vol=0.3  pan=0.4  rev=0.5
voice wonder   celesta   vol=0.45 pan=-0.35 rev=0.6
voice pulse    strings   vol=0.3  pan=0.15 att=0.02 rel=0.1 gate=0.5
voice timpani  timpani   vol=0.6  pan=-0.1
voice kick     kick      vol=0.6
voice snare    snare     vol=0.4  pan=0.1
voice toms     tomlo     vol=0.55 pan=-0.2
voice shaker   shaker    vol=0.3  pan=0.3
voice crash    crash     vol=0.25 pan=0.2
voice choir    voices    vol=0.35 att=0.5 rel=0.8
voice gong     gong      vol=0.35 pan=-0.3

